course: dictionary
lesson: 2082
title: Context clues in history and travel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special place, like history or travel, but context still helps you. «In the Roman Republic citizens elected leaders for one year at a time, and two consuls shared the top job so neither could become too powerful.» The clues are leaders, elected, one year and shared the top job, so a consul must be one of the top leaders.
explain: «Rome had two consuls at the top for that very reason, and a Senate of experienced men to advise them.» The word advise tells you the Senate gave help and ideas. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A leader who is advised, not an adviser.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A consul can be a leader in ancient Rome, or a person a country sends to a foreign city to help its own citizens. Read the sentence around the word to see which meaning fits, just as you would with any other word.
fact: A consul is an official, a person given a job to do for a government.
fact: «Consul» means one of the two top leaders in ancient Rome, chosen each year.
fact: «Consul» can also mean an official sent by a country to live in a foreign city to help its own citizens and look after trade.
fact: In France about two hundred years ago, Napoleon ruled with the title First Consul.
fact: The consulate is the office where a consul works, and travellers who lose a passport abroad can go there for help.
exercise: In «Rome had two consuls at the top», what does consul mean? | A soldier who guards the gates | A loud Roman trumpet | *A top leader in ancient Rome | A kind of Roman bread
exercise: A traveller loses their passport in a foreign city. Who can help them? | A Roman senator from long ago | *The consul or their staff at the consulate | Napoleon | The person who runs the local bakery
exercise: Find and copy one word from «citizens elected leaders» that means chose by voting. | *elected | leaders | citizens | Roman
exercise: Hmm, mention? Test line below.
test: «Napoleon ruled with the title First Consul.» Where and when did this happen? | In a school library, last week | In Scotland, today | *In France, about two hundred years ago | In Rome, two thousand years ago
test: A consul's job is to help citizens of their own country in a foreign city. Which description fits best? | Writing new laws for Scotland | Owning a petrol station abroad | *Helping their own citizens in a foreign city and looking after trade | Ruling ancient Rome alone for life
exam: Why did Rome have two consuls at the top, not just one? | So they could take turns sleeping | Because one was always on holiday | *So neither could become too powerful | So they could be twice as loud
